---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/data';
const issues = 'https://github.com/Mikaaah/TownsAndKingdoms/issues';
---
<Layout title="Issues & suggestions" description="Report a reproducible pack issue, include the right logs or propose an improvement.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Community / Support</p><h1>Report a bug or suggest a feature</h1>
  <p class="intro">Start with what you were trying to do, what happened and how to repeat it. A full log is more useful than a cropped screenshot of the final error.</p>
  <div class="button-row"><a class="button button-primary" href={issues} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Search existing issues</a><a class="button" href="https://discord.gg/CRYk3uDPVt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ask the community</a></div>
  <nav class="toc-inline" aria-label="Support sections"><a href="#logs">Find the logs</a><a href="#report">Prepare a report</a><a href="#suggestions">Suggestions</a></nav>
  <section id="logs" class="section"><h2>Attach the file that answers the question</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">What happened</th><th scope="col">Useful files</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Startup failure or gameplay crash</td><td><code>logs/latest.log</code>, the newest report in <code>crash-reports/</code>, and <code>logs/debug.log</code> if available</td></tr><tr><td>A recipe or script failed</td><td><code>logs/kubejs/server.log</code> and <code>logs/latest.log</code>; include the output item ID</td></tr><tr><td>Client startup scripts or client features failed</td><td>The relevant file under <code>logs/kubejs/</code> together with <code>logs/latest.log</code></td></tr><tr><td>A multiplayer disconnect</td><td>The complete disconnect message and client log; the server log is also useful if the host can provide it</td></tr><tr><td>Persistent server lag</td><td>What was running, when the slowdown occurred and a Spark report if the server administrator recorded one</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="muted log-note">Open the affected instance’s folder in your launcher. Upload the complete text file, or link a readable copy. Review files for passwords or access tokens before sharing them.</p></section>
  <section id="report" class="section"><h2>Prepare a bug report</h2><p class="muted">This form prepares text for GitHub. You review the issue there before posting it.</p>
    <form id="report-form" class="report-form"><div class="report-fields"><label>Short title<input name="title" required maxlength="120" autocomplete="off" placeholder="What stopped working?" /></label><label>Installed pack file<input name="pack" required autocomplete="off" placeholder="The complete filename shown by your launcher" /></label><label>Where did it happen?<select name="side"><option>Single-player</option><option>Multiplayer client</option><option>Dedicated server</option></select></label><label>Relevant item or recipe ID<input name="item" autocomplete="off" placeholder="For example: let_it_walk:walker_core" /></label></div><label>What were you trying to do?<textarea name="goal" required rows="2"></textarea></label><label>Steps to reproduce<textarea name="steps" required rows="4" placeholder="1. Start with…&#10;2. Use…&#10;3. Observe…"></textarea></label><div class="report-fields"><label>Expected result<textarea name="expected" required rows="3"></textarea></label><label>Actual result<textarea name="actual" required rows="3"></textarea></label></div><label>Log, crash report or Spark links<textarea name="logs" rows="2" placeholder="Paste readable links; attach the files on GitHub when needed."></textarea></label><label>Changes or troubleshooting already tried<textarea name="changes" rows="2"></textarea></label><div class="button-row"><button class="button button-primary" type="submit">Prepare report</button><button class="button" type="button" id="copy-report" disabled>Copy report</button><a class="button" id="open-report" href={`${issues}/new`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open GitHub draft</a></div><p id="report-status" class="report-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><label for="report-preview">Report text<textarea id="report-preview" rows="12" readonly spellcheck="false"></textarea></label></form>
    <noscript><p><a href={`${issues}/new`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open a GitHub issue</a> and include your pack file, steps, expected result, actual result and logs.</p></noscript>
  </section>
  <section id="suggestions" class="prose section"><h2>Suggest something worth building</h2><p>Explain the problem the idea would solve, where it fits in the pack and what a player would do differently. For a recipe change, name the current ingredients and the proposed progression stage. For a feature, give one concrete example of using it.</p><div class="button-row"><a class="button" href={`${issues}/new?title=%5BSuggestion%5D%20&body=${encodeURIComponent('## The problem\n\n## Proposed change\n\n## How it fits Towns & Kingdoms\n\n## Example\n')}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open a suggestion draft</a><a class="button" href={href('recipes/')}>Check existing recipes →</a></div></section>
  <script>
    const form = document.getElementById('report-form') as HTMLFormElement | null;
    const preview = document.getElementById('report-preview') as HTMLTextAreaElement | null;
    const copy = document.getElementById('copy-report') as HTMLButtonElement | null;
    const draft = document.getElementById('open-report') as HTMLAnchorElement | null;
    const status = document.getElementById('report-status');
    form?.addEventListener('submit', event => {
      event.preventDefault();
      if (!form.reportValidity()) return;
      const values = new FormData(form);
      const get = (key: string) => String(values.get(key) || '').trim();
      const body = [`## Installation\n${get('pack')}\n${get('side')}`, get('item') ? `## Item or recipe\n${get('item')}` : '', `## Goal\n${get('goal')}`, `## Steps to reproduce\n${get('steps')}`, `## Expected\n${get('expected')}`, `## Actual\n${get('actual')}`, `## Logs\n${get('logs') || 'No log link provided.'}`, `## Changes and troubleshooting\n${get('changes') || 'No additional changes reported.'}`].filter(Boolean).join('\n\n');
      if (preview) preview.value = body;
      if (draft) { const url = new URL('https://github.com/Mikaaah/TownsAndKingdoms/issues/new'); url.searchParams.set('title', get('title')); url.searchParams.set('body', body); draft.href = url.toString(); }
      if (copy) copy.disabled = false;
      if (status) status.textContent = 'Report prepared. Review the text, then copy it or open the GitHub draft.';
    });
    copy?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
      if (!preview?.value) return;
      try { await navigator.clipboard.writeText(preview.value); if (status) status.textContent = 'Report copied.'; }
      catch { preview.focus(); preview.select(); if (status) status.textContent = 'Select the report text and copy it.'; }
    });
  </script>
</Layout>
<style>.report-form{max-width:850px;display:grid;gap:16px;padding:22px;background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius)}.report-form label{display:grid;min-width:0;gap:7px;font-size:14px;color:var(--muted)}.report-fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:16px}.report-form input,.report-form select,.report-form textarea{width:100%;min-width:0;font-size:16px}.report-form textarea{resize:vertical;min-height:70px;background:var(--bg);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:6px;padding:10px 12px;color:var(--text)}.report-form textarea:focus{outline:2px solid var(--focus,var(--gold));outline-offset:2px}.report-status{margin:0;min-height:20px;color:var(--muted);font-size:13px}#report-preview{font-family:ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:14px}.log-note{font-size:16px;margin-top:14px;max-width:850px}@media(max-width:650px){.report-fields{grid-template-columns:1fr}.report-form{padding:16px}}</style>
